# Practical: Develop a Simple Application using AWS Flow Framework

# Step 1: Update the System

Open the **Terminal** and update the Ubuntu system.
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get upgrade
This command updates the system packages.

---

# Step 2: Download AWS CLI

Download AWS CLI using the command:
curl "https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip" -o "awscliv2.zip"

---

# Step 3: Download Signature File

Download the AWS CLI signature verification file.
curl -o awscliv2.sig https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip.sig

---

# Step 4: Extract the Zip File

Unzip the downloaded file.
unzip awscliv2.zip

---

# Step 5: Install AWS CLI

Run the installation command.
sudo ./aws/install

Check installation:
aws --version

---

# Step 6: Install AWS SAM CLI

Install AWS Serverless Application Model CLI.
pip3 install aws-sam-cli

---

# Step 7: Initialize SAM Application

Run the following command to start SAM CLI.
sam init

Select option:
1 - AWS Quick Start Templates

---

# Step 8: Select Hello World Template

Choose the template:
1 - Hello World Example

---

# Step 9: Select Runtime

Type **N** when asked to use most popular runtime.

Check Python version:
python --version

Select runtime accordingly.

Example:
python3.11

---

# Step 10: Select Package Type

Choose package type:
1 - Zip

---

# Step 11: Create Project

Answer **Yes (y)** to configuration options.
Enter project name:
sam-app-test

The template will be downloaded and project folder will be created.

---

# Step 12: Invoke Hello World Function

Move to project folder:
cd sam-app-test

Run the function locally:
sam local invoke "HelloWorldFunction"

Expected Output:

```json
{
"statusCode": 200,
"body": "{\"message\": \"hello world\"}"
}
```

---

# Step 13: Start Local API

Run the API locally.
sam local start-api

It will generate a URL such as:
http://127.0.0.1:3000/hello

Open the URL in a browser.

Output:

```json
{
"message": "hello world"
}
```
